# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("`for`": the gathered event fires with exactly the rows that fired; a row lives while its key is present), ch. 9 (R8: a row ends at the end of the tick its key leaves, having fired in that tick; a request fired by a place torn down in the same tick is still performed) and ch. 4 ("`rebuild`": the events of what left become `never`): in the tick the key leaves both rows ring, afterwards only row 1.
test a_departed_row_is_silent

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="drop")
    1: Ui.Button(label="ring")
    2/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="one")
    2/[1]/1: Test.Log
    2/[2]/0: Ui.Label(text="two")
    2/[2]/1: Test.Log
    3: Ui.Label(text="heard 0")

tick 1
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    3: Ui.Label(text="heard 2")
  requested:
    2/[1]/1: "ring 1"
    2/[2]/1: "ring 2"

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
    1: click
  changed:
    3: Ui.Label(text="heard 4")
  torn down:
    2/[2]/0: Ui.Label(text="two")
    2/[2]/1: Test.Log
  requested:
    2/[1]/1: "ring 1"
    2/[2]/1: "ring 2"

tick 3
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    3: Ui.Label(text="heard 5")
  requested:
    2/[1]/1: "ring 1"
